From 4f1d4d444745a87f057a63fd1ffb732c13276bba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:18:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 280/410] Unified: the Fasteners workbench in the tool search;
 Japanese lists; profiles in whole mm
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- the catalog gives the Fasteners workbench its 223 FS… commands (BIM imports it first
  and took them); "締結部品（Fasteners）" as the module's name; the catalog in the sources has
  them and the shelf's commands
- the hole and what goes in are listed with "、" in Japanese
- a profile placed by clicks is a whole number of millimetres long
- TestPartsShelf: Ctrl+K finds the shelf by ねじ, ボルト, ナット, 座金, ワッシャ, 六角穴付き, M6

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
